{"name":"Oleander Pink","hex":"#f85898","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"oleander","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Nerium oleander, a notoriously poisonous shrub in the dogbane family, Apocynaceae, but nonetheless widely grown as an ornamental, having leathery lance-shaped leaves and deep rose-colored or white flowers."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oleander"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nerium","blocks":[{"text":"Nerium oleander, the oleander, is a shrub or small tree native to the Mediterranean region east to southern Asia, from Morocco and Portugal east to India and Myanmar; the Flora of China also cites it as native in Yunnan in China. It is the only species currently classified in the genus Nerium, belonging to subfamily Apocynoideae of the dogbane family Apocynaceae. It is also cultivated widely in temperate and subtropical areas as an introduced ornamental and landscaping plant."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Nerium_oleander_flowers_leaves.jpg/330px-Nerium_oleander_flowers_leaves.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nerium","wikidata":"Q155833"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.j